        "## Importing Packages\n",
        "\n",
        "Python packages are loaded with `import`.\n",
        "\n",
        "The usual imports in these notes are:"
      ],
      "id": "64aba160"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt"
      ],
      "id": "8b2da5d9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "This means:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `numpy` is used as `np`;\n",
        "- `pandas` is used as `pd`;\n",
        "- `matplotlib.pyplot` is used as `plt`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Specific functions or classes can be imported from a package:"
      ],
      "id": "fa4d891f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split"
      ],
      "id": "c71d78f1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "This is similar in spirit to loading a function from an R package, but Python usually names the module path explicitly.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Data structure\n",
        "\n",
        "### Basic Objects\n",
        "\n",
        "Python has several basic data types."
      ],
      "id": "69dabc62"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x = 3          # integer\n",
        "y = 2.5        # float\n",
        "name = \"tree\"  # string\n",
        "flag = True    # Boolean"
      ],
      "id": "2c1d139a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Use `type()` to check the type of an object."
      ],
      "id": "e95ba942"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "type(y)"
      ],
      "id": "a9f93cb1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Python is case-sensitive. `x` and `X` are different objects.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Lists\n",
        "\n",
        "A list is an ordered collection of objects."
      ],
      "id": "11252155"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "features = [\"age\", \"income\", \"education\"]\n",
        "features"
      ],
      "id": "65cef0aa",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Lists can contain objects of different types, although in data analysis we usually keep them simple."
      ],
      "id": "16fb0c01"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "mixed = [1, \"a\", True]\n",
        "mixed"
      ],
      "id": "21d5f61e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Indexing starts at 0."
      ],
      "id": "23453f22"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "features[0]"
      ],
      "id": "2c6a8ccc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Use negative indexing to count from the end."
      ],
      "id": "cc469486"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "features[-1]"
      ],
      "id": "c8aeaaf2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Slicing uses `start:stop`, where `stop` is not included."
      ],
      "id": "12487cb2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "features[0:2]"
      ],
      "id": "d0167cad",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "This returns the first two elements.\n",
        "\n",
        "Some common list operations are:"
      ],
      "id": "4b646356"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "features.append(\"gender\")\n",
        "len(features)"
