      "id": "38a79edb",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Dictionaries\n",
        "\n",
        "A dictionary stores key-value pairs. It is similar to a named list in R."
      ],
      "id": "2c89c629"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "params = {\n",
        "    \"n_neighbors\": 5,\n",
        "    \"weights\": \"uniform\",\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "params"
      ],
      "id": "d67bdba1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Access a value by its key:"
      ],
      "id": "921365dc"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "params[\"n_neighbors\"]"
      ],
      "id": "7649fee8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Dictionaries are used frequently in `sklearn`, especially for parameter grids."
      ],
      "id": "ad205d3f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "param_grid = {\n",
        "    \"max_depth\": [2, 3, 4],\n",
        "    \"min_samples_leaf\": [1, 5, 10],\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "fc6bb8e6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "For pipelines, parameter names often use two underscores:"
      ],
      "id": "a4596c6e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "param_grid = {\n",
        "    \"model__C\": [0.1, 1, 10],\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "9a432a92",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "This means the parameter `C` inside the pipeline step named `\"model\"`.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### `numpy.array`\n",
        "\n",
        "The most important data structure for numerical computation is `numpy.array`."
      ],
      "id": "91ff0159"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "x = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4])\n",
        "x"
      ],
      "id": "22dab4aa",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "An array has a shape."
      ],
      "id": "2885da03"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x.shape"
      ],
      "id": "4b595de7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "For this object, the shape is `(4,)`. This means it is a one-dimensional array with 4 elements.\n",
        "\n",
        "### One-Dimensional Arrays\n",
        "\n",
        "A one-dimensional array behaves like a vector."
      ],
      "id": "b3c9e933"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x = np.array([10, 20, 30])\n",
        "x.ndim"
      ],
      "id": "fada637d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x.shape"
      ],
      "id": "349fb687",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Indexing is zero-based."
      ],
      "id": "3a607158"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x[0]"
      ],
      "id": "e8602d6f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
